#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:5
#: f223e2c25dd54edaa31414c947b0f395
msgid "Mission Planner Initial SETUP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:6
#: 6d64c5092fda4ce78f3b2ace9fc02165
msgid "This section of Mission Planner, invoked by the Menu item  ``SETUP`` at the top of Mission Planner, has several subsections. The subsections are where you set up and configure your autopilot to prepare it for your particular vehicle. Typically these sections are \"must do\" actions that are required before first flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:8
#: 1d32bbe4b39d43a4977fd40948111ea2
msgid "What you see when you enter this section depends on whether or not you are connected. Each menu item will bring up a new screen, each is discussed below with links to more detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:13
#: da35bac2000c47cb92dd2f5f5ff85cf5
msgid "Install Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:14
#: 0a37212a16c64480a13cefb87ee7dad5
msgid "You will see this menu item if the autopilot is both connected or not; however, this menu will only be functional when disconnected. If you have a new autopilot or if you want to update the control software that resides in your autopilot, you must install (upload) the :ref:`firmware <common-glossary>` into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:16
#: cd9d1326e02840c7afd073afca635f7b
msgid "The firmware is located at `firmware.ardupilot.org <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__. If the autopilot has ArduPilot firmware already installed, you can use this page to upload firmware for different vehicles or versions. See this :ref:`Loading firmware <common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk>` page. Otherwise, you must use other methods than Mission Planner for getting ArduPilot installed for the first time, see this :ref:`section<common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:19
#: 82bab7df89da471a87c5124d5ed1bd3e
msgid "From this screen you can also select \"All Options\" allowing you to select and load any variation of the firmware, or \"Load custom firmware\", most often used when a developer has trial code to load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:22
#: 5291be2484d94d168f35029a7fd8a587
msgid "Install Firmware Legacy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:23
#: 871dd601a283484cb1038a8b731f7e2f
msgid "Yet another way to load older versions of the firmware. Again, shown only when not connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:26
#: e8bd4d3cb47c40dbb4497e2b9eac91ff
msgid "Mandatory Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:27
#: 976d8b4481db4450b72e653590615b0b
msgid "You will only see this menu item if the autopilot is connected. Click this menu item to see the items you must set up before you attempt to operate your vehicle. Specifics are located in the ArduPilot.org documents which cover your specific vehicle (Copter, Plane, Rover, Blimp)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:32
#: 1af0eddaa67542bb8805c92914068fff
msgid "Before operating the vehicle, you must setup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:34
#: 5805839556ec4067aeea5d2b167acfdf
msgid ":ref:`Accel Calibration <common-accelerometer-calibration>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:35
#: 435a2d79df004361aafbb253b8c5021f
msgid ":ref:`Compass (optional for Plane)<common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:36
#: cb68860c362e45e8aad4b9791343fe2b
msgid ":ref:`Radio Calibration<common-radio-control-calibration>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:37
#: 6d037b4b704044d6acde57c7abb6fb7c
msgid "Servo Output : configure each :ref:`output's function<common-rcoutput-mapping>`. Default values get loaded upon initial firmware installation, but be sure to check them here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:38
#: b072bc7a5da94745ae1b77a394c7bee4
msgid ":ref:`ESC Calibration<esc-calibration>` for Copter only (not required for ESCs running DShot protocol, but must be :ref:`configured <common-brushless-escs>` in ArduPilot) Plane and Rover use their own :ref:`common-esc-calibration` technique, but is also a mandatory setup item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:39
#: 282d64e6a4354694aeae01ca187d0695
msgid "Flight Modes: Refer to :ref:`Plane <plane:flight-modes>`, :ref:`Copter <copter:flight-modes>` or :ref:`Rover<rover-control-modes>` mode pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:40
#: 25bec0fdcc8e47ce9cc3a76f9264cf5b
msgid "Failsafe: Refer to :ref:`Plane <apms-failsafe-function>`, :ref:`Copter <failsafe-landing-page>` or :ref:`Rover<rover-failsafes>` failsafe pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:43
#: 8bf966780ad648b3b4766d48cbfb13c9
msgid "Optional Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:44
#: 69df3a039352473a940b5817e0d0b3e1
msgid "This submenu allows the configuration of optional devices, many of which can be configured while Mission Planner is unconnected. Programming of the Sik  Telemetry Radio, UAVCAN setup, PX4 Optical Flow sensor, and Antenna Tracker can be done here, as well as the setup of a :ref:`joystick <common-joystick>` to be used in conjunction with Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:46
#: f35ec47320f5416eb3e6e02d0b11b43d
msgid "When connected, peripherals such as Battery Monitors, Integrated OSD, Airspeed Sensors, and Rangefinders can be configured. Also, this submenu has a Motor Test function allowing you to test the direction and order of Copter and QuadPlane Motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:51
#: 97848630c8564af584086c00910c83ee
msgid "DroneCAN/UAVCAN SLCAN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:52
#: 5571ed9f26994c068167d8c948db7637
msgid "The SLCAN tool inside Mission Planner allows viewing, configuration, and software updates of DroneCAN nodes connected to the CAN bus port of the autopilot. There are two ways to connect to the DroneCAN node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:54
#: 21819c7e00f649c28bc1419dacd6c5ca
msgid "Using SLCAN directly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:55
#: 5db5425bde9142a08acb9b255d366f83
msgid "Using SLCAN over MAVLink"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:58
#: 310a822ca3dc464eabb41882a65cf09f
msgid "Connecting to the DroneCAN node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:60
#: 811d72ae5e0142609d7b345a7175141a
msgid "If using the direct SLCAN connection method, autopilot parameters have to be configured first. See :ref:`common-slcan-f4` or :ref:`common-slcan-f7h7` for setup information. Mission Planner should be in the disconnected state, and make sure the SLCAN port is shown as the selected COM port in the dropdown box in the upper right corner of Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:62
#: cd646e369db04dad999cc70ab8d1f911
msgid "If using the MAVLink method, nothing is required for setup and Mission Planner should be in the connected state via the normal MAVLink connection to the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:64
#: d7445ba267c24a928a231cdaa4e878a4
msgid "In Mission Planner, navigate to Initial Setup->Optional Hardware->DroneCAN/UAVCAN click on the highlighted red button if connecting using the direct SLCAN method, or the appropriate green button for MAVLink communication over either CAN bus port 1 or port 2, depending on which port the node is attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:68
#: 63cbdad51a3345579e62b5bb2cc87e06
msgid "The autopilot will connect to Mission Planner using SLCAN, the window will populate with DroneCAN nodes connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:72
#: d3cfdcf1d6694d9d93114e6a964d5d1a
msgid "If the node has a bootloader only installed, then the firmware will need to be uploaded. ``MAINTENANCE`` will be displayed. Click on update firmware. Firmware can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/AP_Periph/>`__ and downloaded for the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:76
#: 227da4a635314ab2848c6d4921b01c05
msgid "A pop-up will open. Select no and then find firmware for your node previously downloaded and select it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:80
#: 3d76c28d128f47caa56dfd5f6c0543f6
msgid "The window will show the firmware being uploaded and a pop-up will show the status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:86
#: a226ef169752421aabd19eb2f38d3cc8
msgid "Once complete mode will change to ``OPERATIONAL``. Press the ``Parameters`` button to access node settings. From here DroneCAN device parameters can be accessed or changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:90
#: e7bcae82082440aa91811f5941afa3e2
msgid "Clicking on ``Inspector`` will open a popup window to view messages on the CAN bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:94
#: 02b5a586b3144af7ae41eb74f2a7dfa1
msgid "To return to normal Mission Planner operation, change to another tab, and re-connect. You may need to wait 2 seconds before re-connecting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:99
#: 344b8911654040a8a96e2830b5a8a6ee
msgid "DroneCAN Firmware Flashing Video"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:104
#: 00bd90e5cd844adea55993bc83f6cb0a
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:105
#: 7e43ca7198eb4ac18ffc547f170afda9
msgid "This section is for advanced users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:109
#: 79ea47b6572949979fac2a4eee9868c5
msgid "Warning Manager: You can create custom warning messages to be displayed on the HUD and in the messages tab of the DATA screen, based on the values of the status items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:110
#: 17f28bb5e15e45eba4fe4c6731d11d82
msgid "MAVLink Inspector: allows monitoring, real-time, of the various MAVLink status messages being received."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:111
#: 3bc2a61b867a45a585fd9a536ea72665
msgid "Proximity: View the data from a 360 lidar, if equipped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:112
#: 60c620d71f194bc3bc347e7e4315a074
msgid "Mavlink Signing: This allows you to setup :ref:`secure communications<common-MAVLink2-signing>` with the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:113
#: 5c08f8bd9a8d4b849aed06958fdf71e2
msgid "Mavlink mirror: This allows you to forward the MAVLink traffic to another network-connected location for monitoring. Also see :ref:`MAVProxy Forwarding<mavproxy:mavproxy-forwarding>` for another method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:114
#: c9bd60ef5b334023b2e8552310f6b75e
msgid "NMEA: Output the vehicle location as a NMEA GPS string over the network or to a COM port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:115
#: 66ed907da17643f781c7c65735a7e2d6
msgid "Follow Me: If using an attached NEMA mode GPS on a COM port to establish the MP GPS location, can send Guided Mode waypoints to the vehicle to follow the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:116
#: 40276656fd73480d9eec452c6bd6f287
msgid "Param Gen: Regenerates Mission Planners parameter list. Occasionally required if new firmware parameters are not being displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:117
#: 2e481a7492474eb098c79cd35e2c8d11
msgid "Moving Base: if NMEA GPS is attached to PC, shows PCs location as moving on the map display"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:118
#: 652b375854154df3b6664396c7156490
msgid "Anon Log: Allows you to hide your location when sharing log files by creating a version with scrambled locations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-initial-setup.rst:119
#: 3bc56564e5774754aa42dc73d0ae56c4
msgid "FFT: Plot an FFT from a log that has IMU batch sampling enabled. See :ref:`common-imu-notch-filtering` for an example of its use."
msgstr ""
